body:
Slice 6 of 7 of #636. Depends on #658, on #634 (the `retire:` drain walks `scan_page`), and on #662 (637.2, the GC staged-reference slice) for the custodian-side coordination of the dispatch.

## What

- byte-budgeted `drain_step` / `drain_obligation`: cursor-keyed and convergent for a Complete naming >= 4,001 parts. Carried forward from #508's attempts (do not re-earn): one attempt re-derived the same first `B_OPS` keys forever with no cursor; a later one truncated derivation while still marking the obligation fully drained — silent permanent part loss. Regression tests straddle the real boundary, not sit below it;
- `reclaim_owned` with a validated `StagedPlacement` (the discontinued patch decoded `RS(0,0)`, which names no positions — so it marked nothing and then deleted the only record naming those bytes: unreferenced and unevidenced, produced by the reclamation path itself) and single-oversized-entry progress (an entry alone exceeding the budget must still make progress, never re-derive the same shape forever);
- the terminal delete: preconditioned on the session record's exact bytes, gated on the session's `sidx:` range observed empty, exactly-once `mpuctl.count` decrement, slot-range teardown;
- supersede / `unlink` routing through `retire:bytes:{generation}` — flipped in this slice and not earlier, because this slice also lands the drain's production dispatch from `reconcile_step`. The discontinued patch flipped the routing while `drain_obligation` had callers only in tests: an `unlink` of a 30-chunk RS(6,3) object left all 270 fragments resident after GC, permanently — ordinary DELETEs stopped reclaiming space, client-invisibly, and the patch's own classification oracle counted the leaked state as safe.

## Acceptance

- after Complete + drain: `part:` / `psum:` records for published parts are gone and no `orphan:` record names a published chunk;
- `unlink` of a committed object ends, after a reconcile step, with its bytes reclaimed — the anti-regression test for the discontinued run's leak, asserted as a positive reclamation observable;
- a >= 4,001-part drain converges, run twice, with no double decrement; the terminal delete leaves no `sidx:` / `slot:` residue;
- `cargo xtask ci` green.

Part of #636 / #508 / epic #513.
